<title>BELGIUM: Ryanair considers Brussels-London flights.</title>
<headline>Ryanair considers Brussels-London flights.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Irish airline Ryanair plans to launch low-fare flights from &quot;Brussels South&quot; Charleroi airport to London from 1998, the carrier's director of scheduled services Bernard Berger said.</p>
<p>Berger told Reuters in a recent interview Ryanair also wanted to organise a third daily flight from Charleroi, just south of Brussels, to Dublin this winter.</p>
<p>He said Ryanair, which launched its service between Dublin and Charleroi in May, expected to take a 50 percent share of the Brussels-Dublin passenger market in 1998. It expected to carry about 350,000 passengers next year, he said.</p>
<p>The seat occupancy rate on the Charleroi-Dublin line had grown to 75 percent from 60 percent in May, Ryanair said.</p>
